# Line endings and binary safety.
#
# The vendored HID runtime ships prebuilt `.node` binaries. Git's `text=auto`
# heuristics can decide a binary is text and rewrite its line endings on
# checkout, after which `process.dlopen` fails and the plugin reports "driver
# unavailable" on a machine where it installed perfectly. `binary` opts those
# files out of every conversion and diff.
*.node binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.tgz binary

# Everything else is stored with LF so the checked-out tree matches what the
# tarball contains; Windows editors do not need CRLF for Node sources.
* text=auto eol=lf
